# gate-selfcheck G-E — known-benign secret-sweep matches.
#
# Format:  <repo-basename>/<path-glob>   # why this is not a credential
# The reason is MANDATORY. A bare entry is reported as ALLOW-NOREASON, because an
# exemption nobody justified is indistinguishable from an oversight six weeks later.
# Suppression is never silent: gate-selfcheck always prints how many hits this file ate.
#
# Add an entry ONLY after you have looked at the match and can say, in writing, why it
# cannot be a live credential. "It's in a fork" is not a reason. "It's an upstream unit
# test's generated PEM fixture, verified <date>" is.
#
# Established 2026-08-08 (S44) after the first full-corpus sweep: 43 hits, 2 real
# (scrubbed from flowers-marketing, both tokens verified dead first), 41 the entries below.

librechat/*__tests__/*          # upstream fork (danny-avila/LibreChat), not Jason's code: generated PEM keypairs + the literal fixture token ghp_123456… inside CloudFront/MCP unit tests. Read 2026-08-08 S44.
librechat/*.test.ts             # upstream fork: packages/api/src/utils/key.test.ts — PEM fixtures feeding a key-parsing unit test. Read 2026-08-08 S44.
typingmind/src/_next/static/chunks/*.js   # upstream fork: vendored MINIFIED Next.js build output, never hand-edited here. Matches are documented placeholders — AWS's own documentation example key, the AKIA...EXAMPLE one (NOT spelled out here: G-E caught this very file when it was, 2026-08-08) and AIzaxxxxxx… Read 2026-08-08 S44.

braatzio-plan/v3/tools/tenancy-scan.py   # THE PAN DETECTOR ITSELF. Its KNOWN_TEST_VECTORS closed list (three published fixtures — the Visa test PAN, the canonical example SSN, a publicly listed ABA number) and the selftest cases that prove the list is not a loophole. A detector cannot be written without the shapes it detects. Read 2026-09-05 smDrainLedger3-04; the file's own header states the list is CLOSED, and case "a DIFFERENT Luhn-valid Visa number still flags" is the guard.
